.TH XD\-KEYBOARD 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-keyboard \- Keyboard Properties
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-keyboard
.RB [ \-\-page
.IR N ]
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-keyboard
is Windows XP's Keyboard Properties (Control Panel), with the input
languages XP kept in Regional and Language Options:
.TP
.B Speed
Repeat delay and rate (with a box to test them in) and the cursor's blink
rate.
.TP
.B Input Languages
Up to four XKB layouts and variants, the keys that switch between them,
and other XKB options.
.TP
.B Text Services
The input method framework (None, Fcitx 5 or IBus; those installed), which
.BR xd\-compositor (1)
starts when you log on, and Properties... for its own settings
.RB ( fcitx5\-configtool ", " ibus\-setup ),
where its languages and engines are chosen.
The Compose key (an XKB
.B compose:
option).
How to type emoji with the framework chosen; Emoji... opens IBus's
emoji picker
.RB ( "ibus emoji" ).
Choosing a framework also keeps the frameworks' own autostart entries from
starting one in XeonDesktop: a copy in
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart
adds XeonDesktop to their
.BR NotShowIn .
.TP
.B Hardware
The keyboard model, and the keyboards udev knows.
.PP
The lists of layouts, variants, options and models come from
xkeyboard-config.
The settings go to
.IR desktop.ini ,
and
.BR xd\-compositor (1)
applies them to every keyboard at once.
With more than one layout,
.BR xd\-shell (1)
shows XP's Language bar.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " N"
Open the Nth tab, from 0 (Speed).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/xeondesktop/desktop.ini
.B [Keyboard]:
.BR Layout " (e.g. " us,de ),
.BR Variant ,
.BR Options " (e.g. " grp:alt_shift_toggle ),
.BR Model ,
.B RepeatDelay
(milliseconds, default 500),
.B RepeatRate
(per second, default 30) and
.B InputMethod
.RB ( fcitx5 ", " ibus ;
empty for none).
Empty names fall back to the
.B XKB_DEFAULT_*
environment variables.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xd\-intl (1),
.BR xd\-mouse (1),
.BR xkeyboard\-config (7)
